---
description: Never substitute a fallback when a required value or call fails
alwaysApply: true
---

# Never fall back

When a required input is missing or a call fails, stop and print the error. Do not continue on a substitute.

```typescript
// Bad
const rpc = process.env.SEPOLIA_RPC_URL || "https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com";
const token = process.env.PAYMENT_TOKEN ?? "MockDAI";

// Good
const rpc = process.env.SEPOLIA_RPC_URL;
if (rpc === undefined || rpc.trim() === "") {
  throw new Error("SEPOLIA_RPC_URL is required. Set it in .env. See .env.example.");
}
```

- Do not default a name, URL, duration, token, key, command, or address.
- Do not catch an error and retry against a second RPC, token, or code path.
- Do not mint, invent, or mock a missing balance, name, or record.
- The error must name what was missing and the underlying failure.
